Lloyds TSB Bank. Dear Lloyds TSB Bank Customer, The Latest News ALERT MESSAGE: SUSPICIOUS E-MAILS - PHISHING FOR DEBIT CARD NUMBERS AND PASSWORDS: Please be informed that currently fraud e-mails are sent to customers and non - customers of Lloyds TSB Bank requesting to provide their online banking details. In any case you should not provide any of your personal information or banking details. A new Second Level Password (SLP) has been sent to all our Retail customers in your mailbox (online) Please activate the new one.</p Start now the Lloyds TSB Bank Plc authentication process. When you log onto the service we will ask you to accept the updated Terms and Conditions. Once you have accepted these, you will be able to access your accounts in the usual way. Lloyds TSB Bank would never ask you to give through e-mail or any other mean any private and confidential information. If you receive in your mailbox a suspicious e-mail appearing to be sent by Lloyds TSB Bank, please ignore it and contact us now.",i03,Financial Transactions,"GENERAL SETTINGS
